{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536915-hollow-one-child-of-a-technocrat","id":1536915,"title":"Hollow One Child of a Technocrat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-07T19:31:56-07:00","id":1536915,"title":"Hollow One Child of a Technocrat","content":"The Technocrat may end up being NWO, It X, or Syn. The child is just starting high school and never really went to Sleep.<br /> <br /> The question is, when she's using magic, will the Technocrat parent know, and what could the reaction be? Disgust at the Deviant? A desire to lovingly guide (in the WoD? Seriously?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T03:09:34-07:00","id":1536971,"title":"","content":"If the child has always been Awakened, the parent will almost certainly know: there is no way to go 15+ years with someone who has been using Magick concurrently with learning how to walk, to speak, to be potty-trained, and so on. Child mages <i>don't know how to restrain themselves at first, </i>and generally don't even know that they <i>need </i>to until long after the point when they've revealed themselves. If the parent <i>doesn't </i>know, there's something else going on, such as the child having been raised by <i>someone else </i>for most of the formative years. <br /> <br /> If the Technocrat parent <i>isn't </i>hiding the child from the Union (which will be viewed as an act of treachery should it ever come to light), the child will long since have been assimilated and Processed into being a Technocrat, too. Children, even Awakened ones, simply don't have the necessary defense to avoid that. And if the parent <i>is </i>hiding the child from the Union at the risk of life and limb, there very likely <i>is </i>a bond of love there \u2014 as well as a lot of insincerity, since a <i>sincere</i> Technocrat would lovingly guide the child right into the Union for the child's own sake. <br /> <br /> The child also won't be a Hollow One without having a Hollow One mentor: Hollowers and Orphans are two different things; and the Gutter Magick of the Hollow Ones <i>isn't</i> something that comes naturally to mages, despite earlier editions conflating Hollowers and Orphans: it actually takes a lot of ingenuity to make Magick out of cast-away scraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T07:12:06-07:00","id":1536983,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the marriage of the Hollow One's parents broke up early. The parents went on their separate ways and the child was raised by another relative. However, the relative the technocrat thought would raise the child had a crisis and needed to hand the child off to someone else. This relative was loving and responsible but no one a sincere technocrat would choose to raise a child. <br /> <br /> This allows a Hollow One to have a technocrat for a parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:29:56-07:00","id":1537000,"title":"","content":"Maybe a functionary who is a tech based sorcerer and the child awakened in the tween years giving a bit more social support for hiding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:14:51-07:00","id":1537106,"title":"","content":"However it happened for the child to Awaken and become a Hollow One without the parent noticing, this is family matters, so there's no particularly likely answers. It all depends on the specific characters and their relationship.<br /> <br /> Technocrats tend to be highly loyal to the Union due to a number of possible reasons (the less you have completely normal reasons to be loyal, more likely that you went through some processing), but other than that they're as likely to love their children as anyone else. They're also as likely to be disgusted by their life choices as anyone else, or to be supportive.<br /> <br /> At the end it means the answer is all over the place. They're likely to want to stir the child in the &quot;right&quot; direction, but even processed Technocrats don't always think processing is a good thing. Heck, depending on their relationship the parent might even consider defection, or kill their child on sight upon discovering.<br /> <br /> What I can say for sure is that it would be a real challenge to keep your own Awakening a secret from another Mage you live with. Big, but not impossible if the child is at least a teenager by the Awakening, and specially if it is a mutual secret: both more invested on keeping the other from knowing. And a teenager is also highly likely to explore notions their parents don't want them to, so Hollow One wouldn't be unlikely even if they have a scientific upbringing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}